01:07:10.020 --> 01:07:11.020
- Agatha.

01:07:11.020 --> 01:07:12.660
- Yeah, who plays Agatha-
- I don't-

01:07:12.660 --> 01:07:14.480
- She's fabulous.
- Kathryn...

01:07:15.520 --> 01:07:20.007
Whatever her name is,
she does that perfectly.

01:07:21.380 --> 01:07:24.090
She embodies those stereo...

01:07:24.090 --> 01:07:25.801
I mean, Elizabeth Olsen is great in it,

01:07:25.801 --> 01:07:29.260
but Kathryn what's-her-name (chuckles)

01:07:29.260 --> 01:07:32.950
is perfect in the way
that she's able to embody

01:07:32.950 --> 01:07:34.150
those different tropes.

01:07:34.150 --> 01:07:35.910
- But yeah, I think we're getting, I mean,

01:07:35.910 --> 01:07:38.180
if you continue the trajectory,

01:07:38.180 --> 01:07:41.323
and there's so many
comedies now that are...

01:07:41.323 --> 01:07:44.593
They're dramedies, you know?

01:07:47.310 --> 01:07:49.020
That resonates so much with us,

01:07:49.020 --> 01:07:52.943
where you can put funny
people in real situations

01:07:55.060 --> 01:07:57.270
and you can have it all,

01:07:57.270 --> 01:07:59.330
you can have comedy in all those things.

01:07:59.330 --> 01:08:00.163
